        <div class="fc-delta-reason">No second or third Knesset reading of the dissolution bill has been scheduled as of June 14. Election-date negotiations remain unresolved — Netanyahu pushes for October, haredi parties press for September. UTJ formally quit Netanyahu's government over the haredi draft bill dispute (JNS, Jewish Chronicle, Times of Israel), complicating the coalition's ability to advance the bill on its preferred schedule. Haredi-draft and Basic Law Torah Study brinkmanship unresolved. Two readings remain with 31 days to the July 15 deadline and no second reading set. NOTE: UTJ departure evidence from supplementary research source — see judge-notes flag.</div>
        <dl class="fc-meta-row">
          <dt>Resolution</dt><dd>YES if the Knesset passes the dissolution bill in final (third) reading AND that passage specifies a fixed election date earlier than 2026-10-27, before EOD 2026-07-15.</dd>
          <dt>Sources OK</dt><dd>Two TIER1 (Times of Israel/Reuters/AP/JPost) citing the Knesset plenum vote record.</dd>
